## Architecture Guidelines

Use this folder structure unless there is a strong reason to change it:

```txt
app/
  (auth)/
  (tabs)/
components/
constants/
data/
hooks/
lib/
store/
types/
assets/
```

**app/** is for routes and screens only. Screens compose components and call hooks or stores. They should not contain large reusable UI blocks or complex business logic.

**components/** is for reusable UI. Create a component only when it is reused in multiple places, when it makes a screen easier to read, or when it represents a clear UI concept.  Examples for this app: HeadacheCard, or PrimaryButton. Do not create tiny one-off components too early. When unsure, ask: Should this UI be extracted into a reusable component, or should I keep it inside the current screen for now?

**data/** holds hardcoded content. Keep it typed.

**store/** holds Zustand stores. Examples of state to keep here: selected language, user settings, medications, logged headache episodes. Persist with AsyncStorage when needed.

**lib/** holds external service helpers (clerk.ts, api.ts, cn.ts). Never expose secret keys here.

